<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.5 PCT IN SEPT 1-10.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.5 PCT IN SEPT 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by</p>
<p>1.79 billion zlotys, or 1.5 percent, in September 1-10 to</p>
<p>123.42 billion after a 1.7 percent rise in August, preliminary</p>
<p>central bank figures showed.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     SEPT 1-10   AUG     SEPT 95</p>
<p>  change (pct)				1.5	  1.7	 3.5</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   123.42     121.63     90.49</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	22.32	22.09     20.83</p>
<p>  National currency		     101.10	99.54     69.66</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.19	23.04     17.18</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    68.39	67.78     49.20</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
